I find objects, set relationships with ownership and multiplicity, decide each public interface, then

453
00:35:04,321 --> 00:35:05,643
draw the diagram.

454
00:35:06,543 --> 00:35:11,292
If they ask you to explain the pillars of O-O-P, here's thirty seconds. Encapsulation

455
00:35:11,292 --> 00:35:16,041
hides data and gathers the rules about it into the class that owns it.

456
00:35:16,541 --> 00:35:19,421
Abstraction exposes only what callers need.

457
00:35:19,921 --> 00:35:24,168
Inheritance lets a child reuse a parent when child is a parent is truly

458
00:35:24,168 --> 00:35:24,472
correct.

459
00:35:24,972 --> 00:35:30,614
Polymorphism lets one call behave differently per object, which removes type switches.

460
00:35:31,114 --> 00:35:36,743
And in design I prefer interfaces and composition over deep inheritance, use enums for

461
00:35:36,743 --> 00:35:41,970
fixed sets, records for immutable values, and keep equals and hash code consistent.

462
00:35:42,870 --> 00:35:49,042
Self-check. Pause and answer each yourself. What does this, with parentheses, do in a

463
00:35:49,042 --> 00:35:52,569
constructor? Calls another constructor of the same class.

464
00:35:53,069 --> 00:35:58,673
What is dynamic dispatch? The J-V-M choosing an override from the object's actual class

465
00:35:58,673 --> 00:35:59,874
at run time.

466
00:36:00,374 --> 00:36:05,832
Can an interface method have a body? Yes: default, static and private methods.

467
00:36:06,332 --> 00:36:10,936
Where should which spot types fit a truck live? As data on the vehicle

468
00:36:10,936 --> 00:36:11,593
type enum.

469
00:36:12,093 --> 00:36:17,087
The hash code rule in one line? Equal objects must have equal hash codes.

470
00:36:17,587 --> 00:36:24,845
The O-O-A-D steps? Find objects, define relationships, establish interfaces, make the design.

471
00:36:25,745 --> 00:36:30,967
O-O-P bundles data with the only code allowed to change it. Constructors make valid

472
00:36:30,967 --> 00:36:35,070
objects, static means one per class, final means it can't change.

473
00:36:35,570 --> 00:36:41,973
Encapsulation decides who may change data. Abstraction shows callers only what they need. Inheritance

474
00:36:41,973 --> 00:36:48,376
is for true is-a only. Polymorphism means one call, many behaviours, and no type

475
00:36:48,376 --> 00:36:48,833
switches.

476
00:36:49,333 --> 00:36:54,990
Overloading is picked by the compiler from declared types. Overriding is picked by the

477
00:36:54,990 --> 00:36:59,031
J-V-M from the actual object. Fields and statics never dispatch.

478
00:36:59,531 --> 00:37:06,141
Interfaces are contracts, abstract classes share state and skeletons, enums hold data for fixed

479
00:37:06,141 --> 00:37:09,446
sets, and composition beats inheritance for reuse.

480
00:37:09,946 --> 00:37:16,760
Double equals is identity, equals is value, so override hash code with equals. Immutable

481
00:37:16,760 --> 00:37:21,140
records for values, private by default, generics for reuse.

482
00:37:21,640 --> 00:37:27,754
Analysis, then design, then code, and a link with its own data becomes an

